HST Office: every page of the File panel shows its content on Windows, macOS and gen (not only Home).

On the VCL plugins (Windows, macOS, gen; GTK builds its own tree) the File panel showed Home only: Mới, Mở, Thông tin,
Lưu thành, In and Xuất opened blank. The cause is in hstbackstage.ui, not in the layout code: seven self-closing
properties (<property name="label"/> on greeting, recentempty, pinnedempty, newblank, newnd30, saveasfolder and
<property name="uri"/> on moretemplates). VclBuilder reads a property's text with one more xmlreader step; for an
empty element that step consumes the element's end, so its nesting level stays one too high and the siblings after
the object are built inside it. At run time (UITest dump on gen) pagenew was a child of pagehome and the other five
pages children of pagenew: shown, they stayed under a hidden page with no size, whatever ShowPage re-laid out.

- sfx2 hstbackstage.ui: the seven empty properties are removed (the code sets those labels and the link itself, so
  GTK is unchanged); newblank and newnd30 get their Vietnamese label in the file (the code still sets it per
  application) so the accessibility check finds a label; the header comment says why no property may be empty.

License: these upstream-derived files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_ui_empty_properties.py (no empty property in a .ui file the series adds or changes); gen on
Xvfb, every File page has content (tests/runtime/check-backstage-print.py on feat/backstage-print shows the In page).
